ANTEATER POKER
==============

Anteater Poker is an online Texas Hold'em variant for Linux. A server hosts
the table and players connect through graphical clients. The game includes
the Anteater card: in a player's hand it acts as a wildcard, while on the
board it replaces the community cards and advances the game to the final
round.

CUSTOMER PACKAGE
----------------

The precompiled customer package is Poker_Beta.tar.gz.

Extract it:

    tar -xzf Poker_Beta.tar.gz

Start the server in one terminal:

    ./bin/poker_server 10215

Start each graphical client in another terminal:

    ./bin/poker_client localhost 10215

Replace localhost with the server hostname when connecting from another
machine. The first player can start the game after players join; remaining
seats are filled by bots.

The customer package includes the user manual:

    doc/Poker_UserManual.pdf

SOURCE PACKAGE
--------------

The developer source package is Poker_Beta_src.tar.gz. Building requires
Linux, GCC, Make, GTK+ 3 development packages, and Fontconfig development
packages.

Extract and build it:

    tar -xzf Poker_Beta_src.tar.gz
    make

The compiled programs are:

    bin/poker_server
    bin/poker_client

Run the server and client:

    make run-server PORT=10215
    make run-client HOST=localhost PORT=10215

Run the full automated test suite (communication and unit tests):

    make test

Run the test groups individually:

    make test-comm
    make test-unit

The unit tests can also be run one at a time by name:

    make test_card
    make test_deck
    make test_hand
    make test_player
    make test_state
    make test_rules
    make test_game
    make test_monte_carlo
    make test_bot
    make test_poker_protocol
    make test_state_protocol

Run the interactive GUI test:

    make test-gui HOST=localhost PORT=10215

Additional interactive test targets are:

    make test_server PORT=10215
    make test_client HOST=localhost PORT=10215
    make test_gui HOST=localhost PORT=10215

Create the source and customer packages:

    make tar
    make customer_tar

Remove generated executables and archives:

    make clean

The source package includes the user manual and software specification:

    doc/Poker_UserManual.pdf
    doc/Poker_SoftwareSpec.pdf
